<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <head>
        <title>A border with no declared color paints currentColor, and no border paints nothing</title>
        <!-- Engine bug pinned: the raster's default border color was opaque
             BLACK, so widgets acquired phantom black outlines. Per CSS,
             border-color defaults to currentColor; and a box with no border
             declared paints no border at all. -->
        <style type="text/css">
            * { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
            body { width: 800px; background: #ffffff; font-family: sans-serif; }
            .current { width: 300px; height: 80px; margin: 10px;
                       color: #c00000; border: 6px solid; background: #f5f5f5; }
            .plain { width: 300px; height: 80px; margin: 10px; background: #dde8f5; }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <div class="current"></div>
        <div class="plain"></div>
    </body>
</html>
